  "selection": "Existing cheerful adventure BGM and distinct ordinary/Marvy hit sounds are retained. Campaign cues selected from Freesound CC0 searches: Completed.wav for level clear; short 8-Bit Error for failure; C-major bonus-points Happy Ding for three consecutive hits; LevelUp for five. Selection uses uploader descriptions, download/rating signals and measured duration/energy, not a claim of listening. The more-downloaded Victory 1 result was rejected because its description is a crowd screaming rather than a chiptune; a 4.8-second Game Over was rejected as too long for a retry cue.",
  "preparation_command": "python3 assets/music/prepare_audio.py",
  "normalization": "Decode each checksum-pinned source with ffmpeg to 16kHz mono signed 16-bit PCM; apply only manifest-declared end trimming and linear tail fade, then peak-normalize independently to 27852 (85% full scale). The checked-in script records decoded duration, energy distribution and hashes. No runtime normalization or extra PCM allocation.",
  "runtime_mix": "BGM divide by 4; sampled hit divide by 3; BGM ducks to one quarter under effects, with 16 ms ramps. Final mixed samples bounded to +/-16384. Codec master volume 65%.",
  "conversion_tool": "ffmpeg version 7.1.1 Copyright (c) 2000-2025 the FFmpeg developers",
  "campaign_runtime_mix": "Campaign one-shots share the existing divide-by-3 effect gain and BGM ducking/limiter. One cue plays at a time, latest request wins. Clear/fail take main-event dispatch priority over hit/combo; five-hit combo takes priority over three-hit combo."
